# HakiOS fragment: the Infinix GT 10 Pro (X6739, MT6893) -- what is true of this phone and of no other.
#
# The touch screen: this phone has a FocalTech FT3681 on its own I2C0, and the tree's driver for
# the goodix GT9916 and the FocalTech FT3680 over SPI (the POCO X5 Pro's) is of no use here: it
# reads a bus this phone does not have. Both want the same boot argument (touchscreen=1), so both
# would be running at once; the goodix one posts nothing (its reads fail), but it is still a
# driver for a chip that is not in the phone. It is left out of the kernel instead, the way
# devices/qemu/configs/qemu_defconfig leaves out a phone's drivers.
#
# The tree's own driver for this phone's controller is CONFIG_HAKIOS_FT3681
# (drivers/input/hakios.ft3681.c, default y in drivers/input/conf).
CONFIG_DEVICE="x6739"

# CONFIG_HAKIOS_GOODIX is not set

# The data volume: /private/var kept between boots, in the partition `darwin` (the tree's
# configs/persist.config). Without it /private/var is a memory filesystem, empty at every
# boot, and PosterBoard -- which draws the wallpaper -- has nowhere to keep it.
#
# This writes to the phone's storage: the kernel writes only to the partition `darwin`, and
# only from its first block on, and the loader serves the writes. It needs that partition to
# exist (the tree's tools/userdata-carve.py cuts it off the end of Android's userdata, once,
# by hand), so it is left out until the partition is there.
# CONFIG_UFS_WRITE is not set
# CONFIG_VAR_STORE is not set
